The load-bearing wiring. If you change a producer here, audit consumers carefully.

| Producer                              | Consumer                                  | Contract                                                       |
| ------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `bundled-interactives/repository.json` | `package-engine/loader.ts`               | Fallback content when online CDN unavailable                   |
| `docs-retrieval` (`fetchUnifiedContent`) | `context-engine`, `components/docs-panel` | Multi-strategy fetch returns parsed guide                    |
| `context-engine` (`getRecommendations`) | `components/docs-panel`, `Home`          | Returns scored `Recommendation[]` from recommender or bundled  |
| `package-engine` (`createCompositeResolver`) | `docs-retrieval`, `context-engine`  | Bundled-first fallback chain                                   |
| `requirements-manager` (`useGuideRequirements`) | `interactive-engine`, `components/interactive-tutorial` | Prereq verification scoped to the renderer's guide id |
| `interactive-engine` (`useInteractiveElements`) | `components/interactive-tutorial`     | Action execution + auto-completion detection                |
| `lib/dom` (`resolveSelector`)          | `interactive-engine`                     | Selector pipeline: detect → generate → validate → retry        |
| `global-state/sidebar`, `panel-mode`   | `components/docs-panel`, `App`           | Sidebar visibility + content/editor mode                       |
| `security` (`parseUrlSafely`, `validateTutorialUrl`) | All subsystems handling URLs | Boundary validation for any URL crossing trust zones           |
| `learning-paths` (`useGuideCompletion`) | `components/docs-panel`, `interactive-engine` | Progress events + badge unlock                          |
| `recovery` (`evaluateAlignment`)       | `components/docs-panel`                  | One-shot alignment evaluation at guide launch                  |
| `completion-records` (`recordGuideCompletion`, `recordJourneyCompletion`) | `docs-retrieval` (`learning-journey-helpers`) | Single completion-emission boundary; exactly-once per `(kind, guideSource, guideId)` |
| `completion-records` (`armCompletionWriteHook`) | `module.tsx` (`plugin.init`) | Universal plugin bootstrap arms the durable-write subscriber once for every entry surface — nothing is armed and a warn is logged when no user/org identity resolves, so an anonymous session is distinguishable from a broken one and a later identity can still arm |
| `completion-records` (`discardQueuedCompletionWrites`) | `components/LearningPaths` (`MyLearningTab`) | "Reset all progress" drops queued-but-unsent durable writes before its first `await`, so a reset is not followed by records minting for the guides it just cleared |

## Backend architecture (`pkg/`)

The Go backend is a **proxy for the App Platform aggregator**, and nothing else. No database, no
streaming. Direct dependencies are `grafana-plugin-sdk-go` and `grafana/authlib` (the on-behalf-of
token exchange).

The **App Platform** routes (`completion_records.go` + `completion_records_write.go`,
`custom_guide_repository.go`) follow one shape: drain a paginated namespace-scoped upstream LIST,
cache the shaped result per caller, serve it availability-first, and ride the caller's own identity
end to end — outbound as an on-behalf-of access token minted in `pkg/plugin/auth`, never the ID
token itself. Completion records add the write half of that shape: a POST create on the same
coordinate, with identity stamped server-side and a deterministic idempotent name. The canonical
pattern — including the identity trust boundary — is `docs/design/BACKEND_PROXY_PATTERN.md`.

`package_recommendations.go` is the exception and must not be assimilated into that shape: it fetches
a public CDN index anonymously behind a host allowlist, with no namespace and one process-wide
6-hour cache. Because that cache is shared across users, per-user data must never be routed into it.

**File map:**

| File                                | Role                                                                                                              |
| ----------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `main.go`                           | Plugin entrypoint. Calls `app.Manage("grafana-pathfinder-app", plugin.NewApp, ...)`                                |
| `plugin/app.go`                     | `App` struct (implements `instancemgmt.Instance`, `CallResourceHandler`, `CheckHealthHandler`). Holds a logger, the on-behalf-of exchanger, and the completion-write rate limiter. |
| `plugin/resources.go`               | Route table — `http.ServeMux` wrapped in `httpadapter.New` — plus `writeJSON` / `writeError`.                      |
| `plugin/package_recommendations.go` | CDN package-index cache (6h TTL, single-flight dedup, 8-way parallel manifest fetch, bounded memory). Owns `timeNow`. |
| `plugin/completion_records.go`      | Completion Records read proxy (`/completion-records/my`, `/completion-records/capability`). Per-user collation of a full-namespace LIST, 5-min TTL cache with single-flight refresh, invalidation generations, negative-cache cooldown, and stale-serve/503/capability=false error paths. |
| `plugin/completion_records_client.go` | Per-kind wrapper over the shared App Platform client for `completionrecords`: supplies group/version + resource, decodes each `items[].spec` for LISTs, and issues the create (POST) for the write path. |
| `plugin/completion_records_write.go` | Completion Records durable write proxy (`POST /completion-records`). Fails closed on the identity gate, but each status keeps its own shape — rejected → 401 (the client retries after re-auth), while both standing conditions take the structural 404 carrying their own reason token — unverifiable stack → `identity-unverifiable`, no reachable signing-keys endpoint → `signing-keys-unreachable` (neither recovers on retry, so a retryable status would retry to the 30-day horizon and never disarm); server-stamps identity/org/stack/`recordedAt`/`schemaVersion` (`userLogin`/`userDisplayName` come only from the signed ID token's `username`/`name` claims — no fallback, absent claim omits the field and logs); validates a single bounded JSON fact; builds the CRD spec; derives the record name deterministically from the required non-blank client `idempotencyKey` scoped to the trusted `userID` — blank/missing → terminal 400, 409 → idempotent success; clamps out-of-range `durationMs` into `[0, 24h]` rather than dropping the record, and rejects `completedAt` outside `[now−30d, now+5m]`; stales the read cache on success, keeping the entry as the stale-serve fallback; maps outcomes onto the retry contract (201 created / 401 transient after re-auth / structural 404 disarm — persisted data survives, reached by an upstream 404, `obo-unavailable`, `identity-unverifiable`, or `signing-keys-unreachable` / 408+429+5xx+3xx+network+token-exchange-failure transient / 403 disarm with records retained / other 4xx terminal). |
| `plugin/completion_records_write_ratelimit.go` | Per-user token-bucket rate limiter (`newCompletionWriteRateLimiter`, held on `App`) guarding `POST /completion-records` (backend proxy pattern §9 flood guard). |
| `plugin/custom_guide_repository.go` | Namespace-global custom-guide catalogue proxy (`/custom-guide-repository`).                                        |
| `plugin/custom_guide_repository_client.go` | Per-kind wrapper for the guide-catalogue resource.                                                         |
| `plugin/auth/`                      | On-behalf-of token exchange (authlib): mints a short-lived `X-Access-Token` for the calling user from the SSS-provisioned CAP token. `New` returns `(nil, nil)` when no credential is provisioned, so resolvers report `obo-unavailable` instead of failing. |
| `plugin/settings.go`                | Parses `JSONData` and decrypts `SecureJSONData`. Reads only `secureJsonData.accessToken` into `OBOToken`; the exchange namespace comes from plugin-context, not settings. |
| `plugin/app_platform_client.go`     | Shared LIST/create client for App Platform proxies (backend proxy pattern §1, PR #1401): `buildAppPlatformURL`, per-page byte cap + timeout, per-request `X-Access-Token` minting, redirects disabled so a minted credential can never be followed off-origin, two-axis error classification (transient/terminal, namespace-global/caller-scoped), first-request credential diagnostics. |
| `plugin/app_platform_identity.go`   | Shared identity helpers (§3): `validIDToken`, `subjectFromIDToken`, `identityStatus` — fail-closed JWKS signature verification via `pkg/plugin/auth/id_token.go`, bound to the trusted plugin-context namespace (outbound credentials come from `pkg/plugin/auth` too); `deriveCompletionUserID` (the epic's canonical identity contract) delegates here, and `completionWriterIdentity` routes the write path through that same helper. Trust boundary documented in `docs/design/BACKEND_PROXY_PATTERN.md`. |
| `plugin/auth/id_token.go`           | Inbound Grafana ID-token verifier: resolves the token's `kid` against auth-api's JWKS (the Grafana Cloud issuer) and then the stack-local endpoint derived from the Grafana app URL (self-hosted), verifies ES256 signature, token type, and expiry, binds the token's `namespace` claim to the caller-supplied expected namespace by raw equality (auth-api's key set is cell-wide, so the signature alone does not identify the stack; `*` is refused, not matched), and classifies fetch failures for the shared identity gate. Both sources are full signature verification. Each source gets its own slice of the fetch budget, so a stalling one cannot starve the next. A key set that answers without the `kid` is a rejection; only a chain where no source answered reports `signing-keys-unreachable`, and `SigningKeysError` carries the per-source cause so a log line can name the endpoint that failed. The verifier is rebuilt at least every 5 min, so a key removed from JWKS stays trusted for no longer than that. |

**Routes** (all under `/api/plugins/grafana-pathfinder-app/resources/`):

`/package-recommendations`, `/completion-records` (POST create), `/completion-records/my`,
`/completion-records/capability`, `/custom-guide-repository`, `/health`.

**Security boundaries:**

- Package-recommendations URL — `https` + explicit hostname allowlist
- Forwarded ID token — JWKS signature verification, fail closed; never `Cookie`, never a replayed
  `Authorization` header

### What is deliberately NOT here

Sandbox VMs, SSH, the WebSocket relay, and Grafana Live streaming all live in the separate
**`grafana-coda-app`** plugin. Pathfinder keeps the terminal UI only and consumes that plugin's v1
API. `plugin.json` therefore does not set `"streaming": true`, and `pkg/` has no `gorilla/websocket`
or `golang.org/x/crypto` dependency.

If a task mentions `CodaClient`, `RunStream`, `ConnectSSHViaRelay`, `WSConn`, or `resolveVMForUser`,
that work belongs in the `grafana-coda-app` repo. For the frontend side of the integration, load
`.cursor/rules/coda.mdc`; for the operational reference, `docs/developer/CODA.md`.
